<!-- The D.C. Circuit answering brief's Word styles: the cross-engine recipe (tools/fb/src/docxxengine.rs) in the face
     of the typst template (TeX Gyre Schola) at 14 pt (FRAP 32(a)(5); size 28 half points); Body Text and List Item in
     26.4 pt line boxes (typst pitch-double, FRAP 32(a)(4)) with a half-inch indent; quotations, footnotes and the
     heading styles in 17.5 pt boxes (typst pitch-single), quotations 14 pt above and below, 7 pt after each footnote
     (cadc.lua sets every heading's own spacing; the styles give the outline levels). Page setup and footers come from
     cadc.lua's sections and fb render. Twips: 20 x pt. -->
<reference xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships" base="xengine" size="28" body="528" single="350" indent="720" quote="280" note-after="140"/>
